+| PU.48 candidate (`d18531eb…`) live | 36 / 34 / 0.944 | **31 / 31 / 1.000** |
+
+`pump-092` became **correct**: the live path now commits litres `30`, unit price `63.85`, total
+`1915.5` for `30.00` / `63.85` / `1915.5`.
+
+The shipped detector's boxes are tight, so the trim fires on few of them and the live floor holds
+exactly; the annotated path, whose quads are the hand ones, gains a committed cell and a photo. The
+candidate's looser boxes are changed more: five cells that committed before now abstain (gilbarco
+−3, tokheim −2) while `pump-092`'s two wrong cells become right, so coverage falls 36 → 31 at
+precision 1.000. The shipped number is what the app reads, and it is unchanged.
+
+**The brief's candidate baseline does not reproduce on this tree.** The brief and PU.55 both quote
+"41 committed / 39 correct / 0.951" for `d18531eb`; on this commit (82398950, the annotator corpus)
+the same model measures **36 / 34 / 0.944**. The final PU.48 export (`f48991f4…`) measures 25 / 24.
+The 41/39 predates the corpus commit and the `reviewed` set it carries.
+
+### Named mutation
+
+Make the trim always take the full strip (`trimmedToInkBand` returns `(0, height - 1)`):
+
+```
+◇ Suite "PU.58 pump band trim" started.
+◇ Test "a solid bezel band above and below the glyphs does not change the count" started.
+✘ Test "a solid bezel band above and below the glyphs does not change the count" recorded an issue at PumpBandTrimTests.swift:30:13: Expectation failed: onCount == plainCount
+↳ a bezel of 0.1 of the glyph height changed the count to 3
+↳ onCount == plainCount → false
+↳   onCount → 3
+↳   plainCount → 4
+PU.58 the untrimmed slicer breaks at a bezel of 0.1 of the glyph height
+✘ Test "a solid bezel band above and below the glyphs does not change the count" failed after 0.140 seconds with 1 issue.
+✘ Suite "PU.58 pump band trim" failed after 0.140 seconds with 1 issue.
+✘ Test run with 1 test in 1 suite failed after 0.140 seconds with 1 issue.
+```
+
+Restored, the same test is `✔ Test run with 3 tests in 1 suite passed` and the untrimmed break is
+still named at a bezel of 0.1 of the glyph height.
+
+### Found and not fixed
+
+- **The trim's synthetic coverage is 0.05-0.10 of the glyph height.** At 0.15 the LCN flattens the
+  padded strip enough that the faint trailing glyph is not recovered even with the band right. The
+  real ratio (pump-092: 10 rows of 96) sits inside the covered range; a trim read before the LCN
+  would widen it, and was measured and rejected for the harness regression above. No row owns the
+  re-scope.
+- **The candidate's five abstentions.** The trim changes the loose boxes' bands enough that five
+  cells stop committing. Whether that is the trim or the boxes is a detector question (PU.57's
+  tight-IoU gate); the shipped detector is unaffected.
+- **The `PU.23` row-assignment accuracy (0.989 against its 0.99 floor)** and the `PumpSegmentsModel`
+  Python-renderer failure are pre-existing on this tree and touch no slicer code.
